@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: how a workload agent that reads its API key from env gets sbx's placeholder only when the host store backs the key
' covers: internal/sbx/secret.go (APIKeyServices)
' covers: internal/sbx/secret_test.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go (backAPIKeys, storedAPIKeys, Input.StoredAPIKeys)
' covers: internal/run/run.go (StoredAPIKeys wiring)
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/workload_test.go
' see: _spec/internal/sbx/kit-sandbox-credential-gap.puml, _spec/internal/sbx/oauth-provisioning.puml
'
' ── FAILURE (MEASURED 2026-10-27, sbx 0.50.0) ──────────────────────────────
' seed_ready/cursor reached "Press any key to log in" with `cursor (stored)` in
' `sbx secret ls`. Inside the sandbox CURSOR_API_KEY was unset, and
' `cursor-agent models` answered "Authentication required … set CURSOR_API_KEY".
' Same workload with CURSOR_API_KEY set to any placeholder: the model list came
' back — sbx's proxy wrote the real key into Authorization on api2.cursor.sh.
'
' ── UPSTREAM, VERBATIM ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' docker/sbx-kits-contrib cursor/README.md, "What this kit does not own yet":
'   the kit leaves apiKey.proxyManaged off because it "would set CURSOR_API_KEY
'   to the sentinel in every sandbox"; Cursor "treats a set-but-unbacked
'   CURSOR_API_KEY as a real key and reports it invalid", so no sign-in offer.
'   sbx sets CURSOR_API_KEY "only when a host credential exists" — through the
'   BUILT-IN agent's definition, which proveo's own workload (proveo-cursor)
'   replaces since the v3 migration.
' docker/sbx-releases#259 (maintainer): apiKey.name only routes; the
'   placeholder comes from apiKey.proxyManaged: true. Fixed in 0.39; proveo's
'   MinVersion is 0.45.
'
' ── DECISION (user: "Research the correct way to provide a CURSOR_API_KEY") ─
' proveo knows per run what the built-in knew: whether the store backs the key.
'   APIKeyServices   `sbx secret ls` rows whose SECRET column reads "(stored)";
'                    "(oauth configured)" rows are not API keys
'   backAPIKeys      for a copied upstream credential@1 whose service is in
'                    apiKeyEnvWhenBacked and is stored → apiKey.proxyManaged: true
'                    (sbx then sets the env var to its own placeholder)
'   unbacked         left as upstream wrote it → the agent's own sign-in stays
' apiKeyEnvWhenBacked = {cursor}: the one upstream kit that withholds
' proxyManaged for this reason. anthropic and openai stay as they are — their
' kits read SBX_CRED_*_MODE, and an API key outranks a subscription upstream.
title Backed API key → placeholder env, unbacked → sign-in

component "sbx secret ls\ncursor (stored)" as LS <<host>>
component "APIKeyServices" as AKS <<app>>
component "backAPIKeys(caps)" as BACK <<app>>
file "credential@1 cursor\napiKey.name CURSOR_API_KEY\nproxyManaged: true" as CAP <<app>>
component "sandbox env\nCURSOR_API_KEY=<sbx placeholder>" as ENV <<cloud>>
component "sbx proxy\nAuthorization: Bearer <real key>" as PROXY <<host>>

LS --> AKS
AKS --> BACK : stored set
BACK --> CAP : service backed
CAP --> ENV : sbx seeds the placeholder
ENV --> PROXY : request to api2.cursor.sh
note right of BACK
  not backed → upstream untouched:
  the env stays unset and cursor
  offers its own sign-in
end note
@enduml
